# Tracer: inline explicit definition proof
#
# Before (did not parse):
# by def {1} $subset {1}
# Former behavior: `by def` rejected a goal on its header and required:
# by def:
#     ? {1} $subset {1}
#
# Now (verified):
by def {1} $subset {1}
# Current behavior: the inline target uses the same explicit definition checker
# and commit path as the block goal form.
#
# Boundary: only positive concrete props and supported positive builtin definitions
# are accepted; `by def 1 = 1` remains an executable negative Rust regression.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/01_proof_patterns/inline_by_definition.lit
# Implementation: src/parse/by_stmt/definition_by_stmt.rs
